WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Who's involved?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.656
Identity engineers who own
the inbound provisioning job

3
00:00:04.656 --> 00:00:08.212
or the SailPoint Entra source,
and produce the two exports.

4
00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:13.366
The data architect, who decides which
system owns each attribute and reviews

5
00:00:13.366 --> 00:00:18.438
the aliases; Book 3's default keeps
Entra inbound provisioning as the writer.

6
00:00:18.438 --> 00:00:21.713
And the I S S O, who keeps the decisions.

7
00:00:21.713 --> 00:00:23.487
The two reads are read-only.

8
00:00:23.487 --> 00:00:29.137
One wrinkle: SailPoint's policies endpoint
documents the org admin user level,

9
00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:34.420
so a personal token is the wrong tool;
use an API client with one read scope.
